refactor(savepoints): rename Checkpoints -> Save Points EVERYWHERE (no half-rename debt)

Per Mason: a term that means one thing in UI and another in code is debt
before launch. Full rename, all layers:

CODE
- src/checkpoint.rs -> src/savepoint.rs (git mv); mod checkpoint -> mod savepoint
- struct Checkpoint -> SavePoint; all checkpoint:: calls -> savepoint::
- Tauri cmds checkpoint_* -> savepoint_* (snapshot/timeline/rewind/undo/redo/
  get_retention/set_retention/purge) + handler registration + all UI invoke()
  strings (SavePoints.tsx, Settings.tsx) kept in exact sync
- active_checkpoint_root -> active_savepoint_root
- signature "AYGENT Checkpoints" -> "AYGENT Save Points"

UI
- ui/screens/Checkpoints.tsx -> SavePoints.tsx (git mv); component/types renamed
  (Checkpoints->SavePoints, Checkpoint->SavePoint, CheckpointRow->SavePointRow)
- App.tsx import + screen id "checkpoints" -> "savepoints"; Sidebar label/id
- all user-facing copy + comments swept across agents/broker/context_docs/
  conversations/lanes/repo/settings/writer/turns

INTENTIONALLY KEPT (migration boundary, commented at each site):
- on-disk `.aygent/checkpoints.git` shadow-repo path
- git config key `aygent.retentiondays`
Renaming these would ORPHAN every existing user's save-point history +
retention on upgrade. Code is fully renamed AROUND them.

First compile after a cross-cutting rename (module file move + screen-id type
change + 9 cmd renames both sides) — flag if cargo/tsc throws.
